invariant: INV-48
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the four-way round rotates lane 19 by 56 with the other byte
  shuffle, where rho rotates it by 8. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    lanes b13 = lanes_rotate_left_8(a[19]);
--- new
    lanes b13 = lanes_rotate_left_56(a[19]);
